her, it raises the prospect that she may have recorded you or sought to call the authorities after catching you doing whatever you were doing. This was a supposition that investigators and prosecutors agreed with. Toya's phone was never recovered and its movements in conjunction with Singh's car up until he reached a body of water suggested he'd deliberately disposed of it. The obvious explanation for why he'd do such a thing was that there was something on Toya's phone he didn't want anyone to see. Justice Crowley observed that Singh had never shown any remorse and had fled like a gutless coward, harming his own family and prolonging the pain of Toya's loved ones. Then he caused even more suffering by allowing others to fall under suspicion.

