murder in Queensland carries a mandatory life sentence, with the judges then setting a minimum non-parole period that perpetrators must complete. The standard is 20 years, but the aggravating factors in Singh's case led to Justice Crowley sentencing him to a 25-year minimum. Rajwinter Singh has since lodged an appeal which is scheduled to be heard in October 26. Outside of court, Sir Gardner read a statement to the media, expressing gratitude for the police, the community and the verdict, as well as overwhelming grief. Those who loved Toya had been waiting for justice for more than seven years, and they'd finally received it. Quote, Today is a big piece of this journey that needed an ending, and most of all, justice for our Toya. This event turned our

