She should have had so many more. In the years following Toya's murder, multiple memorials to her sprung up throughout the region, a reflection of the incredible mark she left on Far North Queensland. The owners of Canine River Retreat boarding kennels in Karan. where Toya had worked for a time, sectioned off 50 acres of land as part of a permanent walking track, and dubbed it Toya's Walk. Designed as a trail that people could enjoy with their dogs,

